module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LimitApproxClose.Model

/-!
# Charted subalgebras exist, and are cofinal among the finitely generated ones

Let `f : W ⟶ Spec R` be an open immersion with `W` of finite type over the integers, and let
`r : Fin n → R` be a finite family whose standard opens lie inside the image of `f` and cover
it.  This file produces, above any prescribed finitely generated subalgebra `C ⊆ R`, a
subalgebra charted by that family in the sense of `AlgebraicGeometry.IsChartedSubalgebra`, and
packages the result with the two conclusions drawn there: the canonical factorization
`W ⟶ Spec A` is an
open immersion, and its image is the union of the standard opens of the family read inside
`Spec A`.

The second conclusion is what `Stacks.FiniteTypeOpenModel.exists_openModel` of
Tag 01Z7 does not give, and it is the gap the gluing step of the one-affine-open step of Tag 07RN
runs into: the transition morphisms of the glued system are cartesian over the open subsystem
only if the images of the factorizations are inverse images of one another, and that needs the
image of each factorization to be named.

## What is proved, and the route

* `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteType_localization_away_of_basicOpen_le`: a standard open of `Spec R`
  lying inside the image of `f` has a localization of finite type over the integers.  This is
  the only place where finite type of `W` is spent: the standard open lifts through `f` to an
  open subscheme of `W`, which is therefore of finite type over the terminal scheme, and
  Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpenIsoSpecAway` identifies it with the spectrum of the
  localization.  The passage from the terminal scheme to the integers goes through
  `AlgebraicGeometry.specULiftZIsTerminal`, since the terminal scheme is the spectrum of a
  universe-lifted copy of the integers.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_hasAwayNumerators`: a finite generating set of the localization
  gives chart data, by adjoining the element and the numerators of the generators.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge`: finitely many charts and a prescribed
  finitely generated subalgebra are absorbed into one charted subalgebra, by a finite supremum.
  Monotonicity of the chart condition — `AlgebraicGeometry.HasAwayNumerators.mono` — is what
  makes this a one-line transport rather than a re-choice of numerators.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isFiniteTypeOpenModel_opensRange_eq` is the packaged statement: a
  charted subalgebra above `C`, with the open-immersion instance and the image equality.

## Universe situation

The ring and the schemes live in the single universe `u`.  The passage through
`ULift.{u} ℤ` is forced by the terminal scheme of `Scheme.{u}` being the spectrum of a lift of
the integers to `Type u`; nothing else here is universe-sensitive and no index universe enters.

## Transparency gotchas

* `CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.RespectsIso @AlgebraicGeometry.LocallyOfFiniteType` is not
  found by instance search; it is introduced from stability under composition, exactly as in
  `Stacks.FiniteTypeOpenModel.exists_openModel` of Tag 01Z7.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOpenImmersion` of the inclusion of a standard open of `Spec R` is *not*
  found by instance search at this spelling, the open being an open of `PrimeSpectrum R` rather
  than of the carrier of `Spec R`.  It is obtained by rewriting the inclusion as the spectrum of
  the localization map through `AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpenIsoSpecAway_hom_SpecMap`, as in the
  file of Tag 01Z7.

* The finite supremum of subalgebras is finitely generated by induction over the index finset,
  and the induction has to be run on the finset itself and not on the supremum, which no
  induction principle sees.

## What is NOT done here

Nothing here mentions a diagram of schemes, an inverse limit, or
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteTypeApproximation`.  Nothing here chooses the family `r`
compatibly along an inverse system, which is what the gluing of Tag 07RN needs on top of this.
Tag 07RN is not proved and no tag attribute is attached to anything in this file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07RN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Z7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Z7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- **A standard open inside the image of a finite-type open immersion has a finite-type
localization.**  The standard open lifts through the open immersion to an open subscheme of a
scheme of finite type over the integers, and is the spectrum of the localization. -/
lemma finiteType_localization_away_of_basicOpen_le {W : Scheme.{u}} (f : W ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from W)] [IsOpenImmersion f] (a : R)
    (ha : (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen a : (Spec (.of R)).Opens) ≤ f.opensRange) :
    Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (Localization.Away a) := by
  let D : Scheme.{u} := Scheme.Opens.toScheme (X := Spec (.of R)) (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen a)
  let inc : D ⟶ Spec (.of R) := Scheme.Opens.ι _
  have hincOpen : IsOpenImmersion inc := by
    change IsOpenImmersion (Scheme.Opens.ι (X := Spec (.of R)) (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen a))
    rw [← basicOpenIsoSpecAway_hom_SpecMap (R := CommRingCat.of R)]
    infer_instance
  have hinc : Set.range inc ⊆ Set.range f := by
    rintro y ⟨z, rfl⟩
    exact ha z.2
  let g : D ⟶ W := IsOpenImmersion.lift f inc hinc
  have : IsOpenImmersion (g ≫ f) := by rwa [IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac]
  have : IsOpenImmersion g := IsOpenImmersion.of_comp g f
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from D) := by
    rw [← terminal.comp_from g]
    infer_instance
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from (Spec (.of (Localization.Away a)))) := by
    rw [← terminal.comp_from (basicOpenIsoSpecAway (R := CommRingCat.of R) a).inv]
    infer_instance
  let zMap : ULift.{u} ℤ →+* Localization.Away a :=
    (algebraMap ℤ (Localization.Away a)).comp ULift.ringEquiv.toRingHom
  let : Algebra (ULift.{u} ℤ) (Localization.Away a) := zMap.toAlgebra
  let zSpec : Spec (.of (Localization.Away a)) ⟶ Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)) :=
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom zMap)
  have : MorphismProperty.RespectsIso @LocallyOfFiniteType :=
    MorphismProperty.respectsIso_of_isStableUnderComposition
      (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType) (fun _ _ _ _ ↦ inferInstance)
  let eZ := specULiftZIsTerminal.uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal
  have hZ : LocallyOfFiniteType (zSpec ≫ eZ.hom) := by
    rw [show zSpec ≫ eZ.hom = terminal.from _ from Subsingleton.elim _ _]
    infer_instance
  have hzUL : RingHom.FiniteType (algebraMap (ULift.{u} ℤ) (Localization.Away a)) :=
    (HasRingHomProperty.Spec_iff (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType)).mp
      ((MorphismProperty.cancel_right_of_respectsIso
        (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType) zSpec eZ.hom).mp hZ)
  let liftZ : ℤ →+* ULift.{u} ℤ := ULift.ringEquiv.symm.toRingHom
  refine RingHom.finiteType_algebraMap.mp ?_
  convert hzUL.comp (RingHom.FiniteType.of_surjective liftZ ULift.ringEquiv.symm.surjective)
    using 1
  ext x
  simp [liftZ]

/-- **Chart data exists at an element with a finite-type localization.**  Adjoin the element and
the numerators of a finite generating set of the localization. -/
lemma exists_hasAwayNumerators (a : R) (hft : Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (Localization.Away a)) :
    ∃ A : Subalgebra ℤ R, A.FG ∧ a ∈ A ∧ HasAwayNumerators A a := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (hft.out : (⊤ : Subalgebra ℤ (Localization.Away a)).FG)
  have hnums := fun (x : Localization.Away a) (_ : x ∈ s) => IsLocalization.Away.surj a x
  let num : {x // x ∈ s} → R := fun x ↦
    Classical.choose (Classical.choose_spec (hnums x.1 x.2))
  let t : Finset R := insert a (s.attach.image num)
  let A : Subalgebra ℤ R := Algebra.adjoin ℤ (t : Set R)
  refine ⟨A, Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset t,
    Algebra.subset_adjoin (Finset.mem_insert_self a _), s, hs, ?_⟩
  intro x hx
  let y : {x // x ∈ s} := ⟨x, hx⟩
  have hnum_mem : num y ∈ t :=
    Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨y, Finset.mem_attach _ _, rfl⟩)
  let b : A := ⟨num y, Algebra.subset_adjoin hnum_mem⟩
  refine ⟨b, Classical.choose (hnums x hx), ?_⟩
  simpa [b, num, y] using Classical.choose_spec (Classical.choose_spec (hnums x hx))

/-- **A charted subalgebra above any prescribed finitely generated one.**  Finitely many charts
and the prescribed subalgebra are absorbed into a single finite supremum, and the chart condition
is monotone. -/
theorem exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge {n : ℕ} (r : Fin n → R)
    (hft : ∀ l, Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (Localization.Away (r l)))
    (C : Subalgebra ℤ R) (hC : C.FG) :
    ∃ A : Subalgebra ℤ R, IsChartedSubalgebra A r ∧ C ≤ A := by
  classical
  choose A hAfg hAmem hAnum using fun l ↦ exists_hasAwayNumerators (r l) (hft l)
  have hsupFG : (Finset.univ.sup A).FG := by
    induction (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin n)) using Finset.induction with
    | empty => exact Subalgebra.fg_bot
    | @insert i s _ ih =>
      rw [Finset.sup_insert]
      exact (hAfg i).sup ih
  have hle : ∀ l, A l ≤ C ⊔ Finset.univ.sup A := fun l ↦
    (Finset.le_sup (f := A) (Finset.mem_univ l)).trans le_sup_right
  refine ⟨C ⊔ Finset.univ.sup A, ⟨hC.sup hsupFG, fun l ↦ hle l (hAmem l),
    fun l ↦ (hAnum l).mono (hle l)⟩, le_sup_left⟩

/-- **The image equality of the one-affine-open step of Tag 07RN.**  Let `f : W ⟶ Spec R` be an
open immersion with `W` quasi-compact and of finite type over the integers, and let
`r : Fin n → R` have its standard opens inside the image of `f` and covering it.  Then above any
prescribed finitely generated subalgebra `C` there is a finite-type subalgebra `A ⊆ R`
containing the family which is an open model of `f` in the sense of
`Stacks.FiniteTypeOpenModel.IsOpenModel` and whose canonical factorization `W ⟶ Spec A` has
image exactly the union of the standard opens of the family inside `Spec A`.

The lemma `Stacks.FiniteTypeOpenModel.exists_openModel` gives the first two conclusions and
not the third; the third is the one the gluing of the extended inverse system consumes, since
with a compatible choice of the family along the system it makes the images of the
factorizations inverse images of one another. -/
theorem exists_isFiniteTypeOpenModel_opensRange_eq {W : Scheme.{u}} (f : W ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from W)] [IsOpenImmersion f] {n : ℕ} (r : Fin n → R)
    (hrU : ∀ l, (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (r l) : (Spec (.of R)).Opens) ≤ f.opensRange)
    (hcover : f.opensRange ≤ ⨆ l, (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (r l) : (Spec (.of R)).Opens))
    (C : Subalgebra ℤ R) (hC : C.FG) :
    ∃ (A : Subalgebra ℤ R) (hmem : ∀ l, r l ∈ A)
      (_ : IsOpenImmersion (f ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (A.val : A →+* R)))),
      C ≤ A ∧ Stacks.FiniteTypeOpenModel.IsOpenModel f A ∧
        (f ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (A.val : A →+* R))).opensRange =
          (⨆ l, PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (⟨r l, hmem l⟩ : A) : (Spec (.of A)).Opens) := by
  obtain ⟨A, hA, hCA⟩ := exists_isChartedSubalgebra_ge r
    (fun l ↦ finiteType_localization_away_of_basicOpen_le f (r l) (hrU l)) C hC
  exact ⟨A, hA.mem, hA.isOpenImmersion_comp_SpecMap_val hrU hcover, hCA,
    hA.isFiniteTypeOpenModel hrU hcover, hA.opensRange_comp_SpecMap_val hrU hcover⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry
